Handling errors in file operations is important to ensure that a program runs reliably and safely.
File-related errors may occur due to missing files, permission issues, corrupted data, or system limitations.
If these errors are not properly handled, they can cause the application to crash or behave unpredictably.

Reasons for Handling File Operation Errors

Prevents Program Crashes
Proper error handling stops the application from terminating unexpectedly.

Improves Application Stability
Allows the program to continue running or exit gracefully.

Protects Data Integrity
Prevents data loss or corruption during file read/write operations.

Handles Unexpected Conditions
Manages issues like file not found or access denied effectively.

Provides Meaningful Feedback
Helps developers and users understand what went wrong.
